  "caption": "Putting on socks became a workout for Quinn, along with a strange groin ache after long walks. Quinn's theory: walking was wearing the hip out.\n\nHip arthritis often shows up as groin pain, and the first-line approach is usually exercise, education and pacing. Walking isn't the enemy.\n\nWhat often helps: strengthen your glutes, thighs and trunk, keep walking, cycling or swimming within comfort, adjust the dose during flare-ups instead of stopping, and give it 6–12 weeks to notice change.\n\nIf you have night ache, or things are steadily getting more limited, see your GP for a review.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
